        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-266967/blocks/prose-sec-004",
      "source": "sections/sec-004-method.md",
      "source_hash": "9925559d75df9fd584b8a060e75c8e3f2599c2ae3426f02780177dc8ab473d51",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Completes the methods with the pooled vaccine schedule, observation periods and diagnosis of deaths. It outlines the three experiments and presents Experiment 1 results in a table of deaths after treatment with each vaccine alone or with serum.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-266967/blocks/prose-sec-006",
      "source": "sections/sec-006-t-p-subrahmanyan.md",
      "source_hash": "11cdaf6b3a2e05a8d1ba15a765ea3fc1ba8c5c8642595d2f2c1b06afbed202cf",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Reports that in Experiment 1 duck-embryo and HEP Flury vaccines gave little or no protection after infection, while pooled phenolized vaccine with serum protected significantly. Experiment 2 is introduced to compare all three vaccines at identical doses, before and after challenge.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-266967/blocks/prose-sec-007",
      "source": "sections/sec-007-two.md",
      "source_hash": "0b45fe73d6469f07eb7c094b3e114293446c2c660e0ee6438f15911de00abdc7",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Reports that all three vaccines protected when given before challenge, though pooled vaccine did best, while duck-embryo vaccine after infection protected only with one serum. A table gives the Experiment 2 results.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-266967/blocks/prose-sec-008",
      "source": "sections/sec-008-an.md",
      "source_hash": "e620173e27640643c2ec98dd44a92ec03d740c4be32d1e6811792c53e02ce9a0",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes that HEP Flury vaccine after infection gave no significant protection, while pooled vaccine with serum did, outperforming duck-embryo vaccine.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-266967/blocks/prose-sec-009",
      "source": "sections/sec-009-although.md",
      "source_hash": "2f9731c3c79af19db56c7c75e5d73e7e191c8e7da4029ead907df74d1570cbf4",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Reports that, as in Experiment 1, pooled vaccine with serum gave the best results while duck-embryo and HEP Flury vaccines had high mortality and serum alone did not protect. It concludes that pooled phenolized vaccine was superior even at identical doses and introduces a mouse potency comparison in Experiment 3.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-266967/blocks/prose-sec-010",
      "source": "sections/sec-010-the-ed50.md",
      "source_hash": "0118e2091aecc2f624bfc092826e5ca0a69c644600c1b80cc2120287e3b91d42",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Reports that duck-embryo vaccines were weaker antigens than pooled vaccine in mouse potency tests, though they passed against an outdated reference vaccine. The discussion criticizes earlier protection studies of duck-embryo vaccine for using very large doses unrelated to human treatment.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-266967/blocks/prose-sec-011",
      "source": "sections/sec-011-n-veeraraghavan-t-p-subrahmanyan.md",
      "source_hash": "4aaea7158a7d368b0ab75aa323a439d7a5c01c5efa090ee2eb05b0b6aa9b9745",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "A fragment saying that large doses and delayed challenge could explain good results in an earlier experiment.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
