    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-266967/blocks/prose-sec-012",
      "source": "sections/sec-012-and.md",
      "source_hash": "00625c85c7b8afb6cfbca86bd989191a8fe91f5622186a7a7e6637ec3c9b5514",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Lists further flaws in earlier studies, such as timing and route of challenge, few animals and short observation, and explains how the present study avoided them. It argues that the dose of duck-embryo vaccine needed would be unaffordable for countries such as India. The mouse potency results are said to support the protection findings.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-266967/blocks/prose-sec-013",
      "source": "sections/sec-013-minimum.md",
      "source_hash": "4e7c4610c90b4422f2de1a859d6e11fed9b37f59202f252bfcfd6430a7094477",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes agreement with other findings that many duck-embryo vaccine lots fail potency requirements, and judges HEP Flury vaccine too poor for post-infection use. The conclusions restate that the recommended human dose of duck-embryo vaccine is inadequate and that nervous tissue vaccines should be replaced only after careful studies.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
